t."],[765,"The Popover component is an overlay element positioned relative to a trigger element."],[71,"The primary button should be used to indicate the most important action for the user to take in their current experience."],[933,"The range configuration is invalid"],[1545,"The rounding prop sets border-radius. Use `full` for fully rounded corners."],[72,"The secondary button indicates an action of secondary importance."],[1004,"The segmented controller follows the current layout direction (LTR or RTL), detected automatically from the browser or system settings."],[1532,"The spacing props use semantic t-shirt sizes for padding, gap, and other spacing properties:"],[382,"The states **disabled**, **readonly**, and **invalid** are applied by the field wrapper (e.g. TextField, NumberField, Select). The group reflects them via data attributes on the group."],[73,"The tertiary button is the default, low-emphasis style used for common, non-critical actions."],[1289,"The Tooltip component displays a description of an element on hover or focus."],[1308,"The tooltip uses `role=\"tooltip\"` and is associated with its focusable element via `aria-describedby`."],[667,"The tooltip uses `role=\"tooltip\"` and is associated with the info trigger via `aria-describedby`."],[1090,"The track and thumb read from Antares curated tokens, falling back to legacy `--ux-*` custom properties:"],[931,"The value or endpoint labels are blank"],[271,"The whole field is a single focusable button; Enter/Space opens the popover"],[482,"These are re-exports of the underlying Bento Icon system methods. For complete API documentation, advanced usage patterns, and implementation details, see the `@bento/icon` and `@bento/svg-parser` package documentation."],[15,"This also works with autocomplete in IDEs and LLMs, so you can import from the root package and let your editor/agent suggest the available components."],[514,"This approach works well for SSR and small numbers of icons, but can lead to DOM bl